A||||4||sid1200||poly bushings||||1||
Z||000000||sid1200||05-22-2000||07:00 PM||||Hi, just jacked up my 88 GT and am wondering if I have poly bushings on it.<P>the bushings are hard and yellow in color.  don't feel like rubber  ( I think what I saw where the bushings), at least on the back of the car<P>I've been having squeking problems with them, so any advice on what this stuff is and how to stop the squeaks would be great.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-23-2000||01:19 AM||||If they are not black rubber they could be poly. Poly does make sqeaks and groans. I think someone mentioned previously they used graphite to quiet the noises. You can do a search on poly bushings or check the archives.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||05-23-2000||05:22 PM||||Which bushings are we talking about? Cradle bushings, Control arm bushings?  The cradle bushings are on the four corners of the cradle.  Two up front where the cradle mounts to the car, near the coolant lines under the fire wall. These have a nut and bolt going through them side ways.  The other two are by the trunk of the car going up.  They are harder to see and there is only a bolt (no nut)going through the cradle and bushing into the frame. <BR>  As was mentioned, if they are not black most likely they are polyurethane.<P>  I also have polyurethane bushings on my control arms, and on my tie rod boots.  Less movement than the rubber ones.  Last longer too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||05-23-2000||08:00 PM||||Jay, sid1200 has an 88GT and the 88's don't have bushings on all the corners. The 88's are solid mounted, but you are right because all other years the fiero has cradle bushings. sid1200 if you saw the bushings on the sway bar or coming of the sway bar, those are normally yellow in color. I remember seenig your bushings and they are black and the are made of rubber. Sorry had to put my .02 cents worth.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jay||05-25-2000||04:08 PM||||Sorry, must have missed that 88 thing.||||reg||1
